---
import { caseStudyMotionTokens, caseStudyPresentationTokens } from '../scripts/case-study/case-study-motion';
interface Props { inventory: ReturnType<typeof import('../data/system-inventory').buildSystemInventory>; }
const { inventory } = Astro.props;
---
<section id="case-study-transition" class="ds-section"><header class="ds-heading"><h2>Case-study transition</h2><p>A project card opens the same case study as its direct page. Closing returns the reader to the original card, position and focus.</p></header>
  <div class="ds-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Token</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead><tbody>{[...caseStudyMotionTokens,...caseStudyPresentationTokens].map(token => <tr><th>{token.label}</th><td><a href={`#token-${token.name.slice(2)}`}><code>{token.name}</code></a></td><td>{inventory.palettes.light[token.name.slice(2)]}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <p>Keyboard close, Escape and browser Back restore focus. Reduced motion opens and closes immediately. Videos and images keep their existing playback and source.</p>
</section>
<section id="floating-header" class="ds-section"><header class="ds-heading"><h2>Floating header</h2><p>The wordmark, links and theme control stay together when the header becomes a floating pill. The navigation follows the page theme.</p></header><p>Use the website’s SiteHeader and NavigationItem. Keep the mobile menu’s keyboard access and focus return.</p></section>
<section id="work-filter" class="ds-section"><header class="ds-heading"><h2>Work filter</h2><p>Readers choose Selected work, Websites or Misc. The selected category stays in the URL and the result count is announced.</p></header><p>Use SectionNavigation with WorkSection. Preserve source order, keyboard focus and the existing reduced-motion behavior.</p></section>
